    {
      "title": "Module 1 \u00b7 Basic Definitions",
      "html": "<p>Probability of an event $E$:</p>$$P(E) = \\dfrac{n(E)}{n(S)}$$<p>where $S$ is the sample space. Always $0 \\le P(E) \\le 1$. $P(\\text{not }E) = 1 - P(E)$.</p><h4>Key points</h4><ul><li>One favourable outcome out of 6.</li><li>Even: 2, 4, 6 \u2014 three outcomes out of 6.</li></ul><h4>Worked example</h4><p><b>Q:</b> A fair die is thrown. Find P(a 3).<br/><b>A:</b> \\dfrac{1}{6}</p><p><b>Q:</b> A fair die is thrown. Find P(an even number).<br/><b>A:</b> \\dfrac{1}{2}</p>",
      "examples": [
        {
          "q": "A fair die is thrown. Find P(getting a 4).",
          "a": "$P = 1/6$."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Module 2 \u00b7 Laws of Probability",
      "html": "<p><b>Addition law:</b> $P(A\\cup B) = P(A) + P(B) - P(A\\cap B)$. If $A,B$ are <b>mutually exclusive</b>: $P(A\\cup B) = P(A) + P(B)$.</p><p><b>Multiplication law:</b> If $A,B$ are <b>independent</b>: $P(A\\cap B) = P(A)P(B)$. If dependent: $P(A\\cap B) = P(A)P(B|A)$.</p><h4>Key points</h4><ul><li>The complement's probability.</li></ul><h4>Worked example</h4><p><b>Q:</b> What is $P(\\text{not }E)$ in terms of $P(E)$?<br/><b>A:</b> 1-P(E)</p><h4>More key points</h4><ul><li>Probability of obtaining a head in a toss of a coin. \u2014 1/2.</li><li>The range of probability is: \u2014 0 to 1.</li><li>Find the probability of picking a queen from a standard deck of 52 cards. \u2014 1/13.</li><li>A bag contains 4 red and 6 black balls. If two balls are picked without replacement, find the probability both are red. \u2014 2/15.</li></ul>",
      "examples": [
        {
          "q": "A card is drawn from a pack. Find P(King or Queen).",
          "a": "$P = 4/52 + 4/52 = 8/52 = 2/13$."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Module 3 \u00b7 Tree Diagrams",
      "html": "<p>Branches represent each possible outcome; multiply along branches, add between branches.</p><h4>Key points</h4><ul><li>One favourable outcome out of 6.</li><li>Even: 2, 4, 6 \u2014 three outcomes out of 6.</li></ul><h4>Worked example</h4><p><b>Q:</b> A fair die is thrown. Find P(a 3).<br/><b>A:</b> \\dfrac{1}{6}</p><p><b>Q:</b> A fair die is thrown. Find P(an even number).<br/><b>A:</b> \\dfrac{1}{2}</p>",
      "examples": [
        {
          "q": "A bag contains 3 red and 5 blue balls. Two balls are drawn without replacement. Find P(both red).",
          "a": "$P = \\dfrac{3}{8}\\times \\dfrac{2}{7} = \\dfrac{6}{56} = \\dfrac{3}{28}$."
        }
      ]
    },
