      "html": "<p><b>Sample space and outcomes</b> is a key part of Probability (SSS 3, Mathematics). Master the meaning, the main points and how it is tested in JAMB and WAEC questions on this topic.</p><h4>Key points</h4><ul><li>Probability of an event $E$: $$P(E) = \\dfrac{n(E)}{n(S)}$$ where $S$ is the sample space.</li><li>Even: 2, 4, 6 \u2014 three outcomes out of 6.</li></ul><h4>Worked example</h4><p><b>Q:</b> A fair die is thrown. Find P(an even number).<br/><b>A:</b> \\dfrac{1}{2} \u2014 Even: 2, 4, 6 \u2014 three outcomes out of 6.</p>",
      "examples": [
